Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: coreutils, procps, {{ DEPS }}
Description: vendor-generic GPU passthrough glue for Proxmox LXC guests
 Prints or applies the lxc.conf lines that expose a GPU to an LXC guest, for
 every vendor: the shared /dev/dri subtree for AMD and Intel, the /dev/nvidia*
 character devices plus the proprietary user-space libraries for NVIDIA.
 .
 The tool probes the actual host at runtime — device nodes, majors and library
 paths are read from the machine running it, so no vendor table is hardcoded
 and adding a new GPU of an already-covered vendor needs no package change.
 Lines are idempotent on --apply (already-present lines are skipped) and the
 default mode writes nothing: every --apply call is a deliberate operator
 step. See the wiki GPU-Support page for the vendor x level matrix.
